  "contract": [
    "Phase 2 of the subsurface design: ore bodies by deposit type (organic, marine, continental, hydrothermal, magmatic, metamorphic), each with its minerals from GregTech CE Unofficial 2.8.10-beta overworld materials, Supersymmetry's overworld minerals (Riven ore blocks; riven-content.json) and Riven's seam and rock blocks. source names where a deposit's mineral set comes from: susy (Supersymmetry's overworld veins and deposits), gtceu (GTCEu's overworld veins) or riven (composed by Riven). Every body is a pure function of seed, definitions and coordinates; GTCEu's world generator never runs.",
    "Origins. lens: a stratiform sheet inside a host unit, one per cell (cellBlocks, chance), radiusBlocks wide and thicknessBlocks thick at its centre, tapering to its rim, at a fixed fraction of the host unit's whole thickness (the part eroded above the surface included) so it follows the bed through folds and faults and the land cuts it. sheet: a planar vein from a cell, lengthBlocks along strike and heightBlocks along dip (half extents, elliptical), thicknessBlocks thick, dipping dipDegrees, kept only inside host units. contact: a band bandBlocks thick on the host side wherever a host unit meets a partner unit above or below it, inside a cell's patch radiusBlocks wide; with aureoleBlocks, also every host block within that many blocks (wobbling along the wall) outside a pluton's wall and below its rim roof. pipe: every host block. Bodies apply only between y[0] and y[1] and, with maxDepthBlocks, no deeper than that below the surface; a column holds at most maximumBodies bodies, earlier deposits winning.",
    "fill: solid bodies (seams and rock bodies) fill their whole interval: sporadicShare of blocks take the sporadic mineral, the rest take primary above primaryAbove of the body's height, secondary below secondaryBelow and between in the middle. Other bodies grow ore nodes: a jittered 3D grid of cells nodes.cellBlocks wide may hold one node each, a lumpy ellipsoid (axes varied by shapeVariation at constant volume) of orePerNode blocks, or megaOrePerNode at megaChance; a node forms in a body with the deposit's nodeChance times densityScale, times 1 + deepGain scaled from deepGainFromY (none) to deepGainToY (full), when its centre lies in the body padded by padBlocks above and below, and keeps its whole volume. Each node is one mineral, by its centre's height in the body, sporadicShare of nodes taking the sporadic mineral.",
    "minerals: the vanilla ore each mineral becomes without GTCEu or Riven's ore blocks (NONE leaves the rock). blocks: minerals that are always a Riven block (seams, evaporites, placers, rock bodies) in any host. Otherwise, in Riven's host stones a mineral is its Riven ore block (riven-content.json ores); elsewhere its GTCEu ore in the host's stone type (stone for sandstone), or its vanilla fallback. Ores replace a bed's own rock only in native cubes, below the cover the surface rules lay (soil, sand, beach, bar and slope gravel, the sandstone under sand); caves, water, lava and the distant preview are unchanged."
  ]
}
